# Benchmark build cache + downloaded datasets — large, regenerable, NOT committed.
# The brain bench harnesses (benchmark/scripts/*.mjs) build a Rust IPC bin and
# download datasets (LongMemEval-S, LoCoMo) into here. Results worth keeping are
# written to benchmark/results/ (committed); everything below is scratch.
.cache/
target-bench/
bench-results/

# Python bytecode caches from the Python harnesses (embedder-sweep, arc-agi-2).
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Transient per-attempt raw logs can get large; keep curated results + summaries.
# (raw_*.jsonl under results/ are committed evidence — do NOT ignore those.)

# Heavy per-query retrieval-DETAIL JSON from the LoCoMo MTEB harness (40-60 MB) —
# fully reproducible; the committed .md summary carries the headline numbers that
# COMPARISON.md cites, so we keep the .md and ignore the heavy .json.
# NOTE: longmemeval_s_terransoul.json (~1.8 MB) IS committed as raw evidence for
# the LongMemEval-S row in COMPARISON.md.
results/locomo_mteb_terransoul*.json

# External-system bench scratch stores (Chroma/SQLite indexes rebuilt per run).
results/external-systems/.mem0_chroma/
results/external-systems/*.sqlite
results/external-systems/.cognee*/

results/external-systems/.hipporag_smoke/
results/external-systems/.hipporag_store/
results/external-systems/*_venv/
results/external-systems/.*_venv/
results/external-systems/.amem_chroma/
results/external-systems/.*chroma/
results/external-systems/.memary*/
results/longmemeval_s_terransoul_*.json
